# CUEMS gradient-motiond — per-node environment overrides.
#
# Read by cuems-gradient-motiond.service via
# EnvironmentFile=-/etc/cuems/gradient-motiond.env. The unit sets a
# default CUEMS_GRADIENT_OSC_PORT=7100; values here override that default.
#
# How to use:
#   1. Copy this file to /etc/cuems/gradient-motiond.env
#   2. Uncomment and set the variables you need
#   3. sudo systemctl restart cuems-gradient-motiond
#
# To disable overrides: remove /etc/cuems/gradient-motiond.env (the leading
# `-` on the service's EnvironmentFile makes a missing file OK).

# UDP OSC listen port (gradient-motion-engine v0.3.0+)
#CUEMS_GRADIENT_OSC_PORT=7100

# Other CLI options (e.g. --node-name for OSC node_name filter, different
# --midi-port) are not read from this file — use a drop-in instead:
#   sudo systemctl edit cuems-gradient-motiond
#   [Service]
#   ExecStart=
#   ExecStart=/usr/bin/gradient-motiond --midi-port "Your Port" \
#       --osc-port $CUEMS_GRADIENT_OSC_PORT --log-level info --node-name node-002
